NAME
    diff - show the lines that differ between two files

SYNOPSIS
    diff file1 file2

DESCRIPTION
    Skips the lines the files share at the start and at the end and
    prints the block between: the lines only in file1 prefixed "< ",
    then those only in file2 prefixed "> ". Identical files print
    nothing. One changed, inserted or deleted block comes out exact;
    several changes come out as one block spanning them (this is not a
    minimal diff). diff is /BIN/DIFF.

    Errors: "diff: file1 not found", "diff: file2 not found".

LIMITS
    Each file is held in memory: 150 lines of 79 characters (CR is
    dropped, longer lines are cut). A longer file is compared on its
    first 150 lines, and diff says "diff: only the first 150 lines were
    compared".

EXAMPLES
    diff /FRUIT.TXT /FRUIT2.TXT    < banana 12 yellow
                                   > kiwi 9 brown

NOTES
    Changed from the P8X version: 150 lines per file (was 96) and the
    warning for a longer file.
    Ported from P8X os/commands/diff.c 2026-09-23.

SEE ALSO
    cmp, cat, grep
